From: =?UTF-8?q?Maxime=20M=C3=A9r=C3=A9?= <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Date: Thu, 7 May 2026 17:40:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 450/913] drivers: stm32_tamp: drain pending events before IRQ
 enable
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Call the tamper interrupt handler before enabling IER so events latched
during early boot are handled with the configured callbacks.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git a0bbbf4559d314b2412f0d8e6288421cf9258415 drivers: stm32_tamp: drain pending events before IRQ enable]
Signed-off-by: Maxime Méré <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: Ib2179dff8f806c7b250e2aa5dd4df194018f5750
---
 core/drivers/stm32_tamp.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/core/drivers/stm32_tamp.c b/core/drivers/stm32_tamp.c
index e354505c9..fc05a4b9e 100644
--- a/core/drivers/stm32_tamp.c
+++ b/core/drivers/stm32_tamp.c
@@ -1417,6 +1417,9 @@ static TEE_Result stm32_tamp_set_config(void)
 		}
 	}
 
+	/* Drain any tamper event latched before interrupt enable. */
+	stm32_tamp_it_handler(stm32_tamp_dev->pdata.itr);
+
 	/* Enable interrupts. */
 	io_write32(base + _TAMP_IER, ier);
 
-- 
